rust	UNKNOWN STEP	
rust	UNKNOWN STEP	## For humans
rust	UNKNOWN STEP	A message you send on the Threads screen now shows once, from the tap until the orchestrator answers, with its photo and its ✓.
rust	UNKNOWN STEP	Before, a second copy of the same message (and photo) could appear right after sending and stay until the thread next refreshed.
rust	UNKNOWN STEP	
rust	UNKNOWN STEP	## What was wrong
rust	UNKNOWN STEP	There is no separate pending bubble: both copies were the same logged message. After a send the page reloads the thread (300 ms later) while its live stream also announces the new message as an `insert`. When the stream's insert landed after the reload, the page added it a second time, because applying an `insert` never checked whether that block was already there.
rust	UNKNOWN STEP	
rust	UNKNOWN STEP	## Fix
rust	UNKNOWN STEP	`web/src/ops.ts`: an `insert` whose target list exists first drops any block with the same id, so applying it twice is the same as once (the server's newer copy wins, in its place). `web/dist/board.js` rebuilt with `npm run build`.
rust	UNKNOWN STEP	
rust	UNKNOWN STEP	No client nonce: the two copies already share one id (`m-<seq>`); matching on it is enough, and no composer change was needed.
rust	UNKNOWN STEP	
rust	UNKNOWN STEP	## Repro
rust	UNKNOWN STEP	This test needs WebKit, and only CI's ui-webkit job has it: lanes may not install a browser, and CI runs only on pull requests, so commit 1 on its own (54d7c0f7) never got a WebKit run. Head passing is the ui-webkit job at a34b663e83560b8f395de129c90ee5bd0cebaf6a. The failure on base + commit 1 needs the verify stage or a host with Playwright WebKit.
rust	UNKNOWN STEP	
rust	UNKNOWN STEP	Commit 1, 54d7c0f7: `cargo test -p drover --test threads_tab a_sent_message_with_a_photo_shows_once_from_tap_to_echo_in_webkit_at_390`: WebKit at 390 on a real `serve`, the stream delayed 1.5 s (a slow phone link) so its insert lands after the reload; sends a message with a photo, counts matching bubbles on every DOM mutation, expects `[most 1, one after echo, its ✓, its photo]`. On the base the stream insert adds a second bubble (most = 2).
rust	UNKNOWN STEP	
rust	UNKNOWN STEP	## Round 5 (update onto staging) at head bf0964d896c07c9ab5d99de7335dfac3fea49a04
rust	UNKNOWN STEP	Merged `origin/staging` (conflict in generated `web/dist/board.js` only); resolved by rebuilding it from the merged `web/src`, not by hand.
rust	UNKNOWN STEP	- `npm ci && npm run build && npm run check && npm run lint` in web/: exit 0.
rust	UNKNOWN STEP	- `cargo fmt --check`: exit 0. CI's two `cargo clippy` commands: exit 0.
rust	UNKNOWN STEP	- `cargo test --locked -p drover --test threads_tab`: exit 0 (17 passed).
rust	UNKNOWN STEP	- `cargo test --locked --workspace`: exit 101, one failure, `shed.rs` `a_missing_shed_is_named_by_spawn_and_doctor_and_timer_install_adds_it`: it expects `shed` off PATH, but this lane host has it in `~/.cargo/bin`. This PR does not touch shed (its diff vs staging is threads_tab.rs, ops.ts, board.js).
rust	UNKNOWN STEP	
rust	UNKNOWN STEP	## Round 4 (review fix) at head a34b663e83560b8f395de129c90ee5bd0cebaf6a
rust	UNKNOWN STEP	- `web/src/ops.ts`: an insert drops an earlier copy only when the block has an id, so an insert with no id leaves its id-less siblings alone (reviewer's non-blocking finding). `web/dist/board.js` rebuilt.
rust	UNKNOWN STEP	- `npm ci && npm run build && npm run check && npm run lint` in web/: exit 0 each. Before the change, a rebuild at 0e9efed6 left web/dist unchanged.
